The contract has a useful finite domain insight: “even digits” means the only possible outputs are `2, 4, 6, 8`; values such as `10–14` produce none. I’m implementing the function as ordered membership checks for those four digits. That keeps the Python within the translator’s subset and makes the universal proof finite over arbitrary positive integer endpoints.
